  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/d08789b320b5d3f4851d5b63019c869051e76ff8</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/pekoqq/ReadLoops/commit/d08789b320b5d3f4851d5b63019c869051e76ff8"/>
    <title>
        polish(ui): damped curve + kill the second source of ghosting
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-13T22:20:53Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/b0b053e92a161bc8889ef2418899d68b?d=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.githubassets.com%2Fimages%2Fgravatars%2Fgravatar-user-420.png&amp;r=g&amp;s=30"/>
    <author>
      <name></name>
      <email>readloops-dev@users.noreply.github.com</email>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;polish(ui): damped curve + kill the second source of ghosting

- #reader.page-fading used a transition; removing it tweened opacity back to
  1 while page-enter started from 0, briefly showing the old frame. Both
  phases are animations now.
- new --ease-damped cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.28, 0.42, 1): a real overshoot that
  settles back
- content entrance 0.68 -&amp;gt; 0.78s, lift 14px, stagger 0.055s
- page leave 0.16 -&amp;gt; 0.10s so the old page never lingers&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/172fc0e491d4ccf5cf3e8ee9cd84ff240f2a42a0</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/pekoqq/ReadLoops/commit/172fc0e491d4ccf5cf3e8ee9cd84ff240f2a42a0"/>
    <title>
        fix(ui): eliminate page-switch ghosting; add damping to entrances
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-13T22:02:32Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://0.gravatar.com/avatar/b0b053e92a161bc8889ef2418899d68b?d=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.githubassets.com%2Fimages%2Fgravatars%2Fgravatar-user-420.png&amp;r=g&amp;s=30"/>
    <author>
      <name></name>
      <email>readloops-dev@users.noreply.github.com</email>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;fix(ui): eliminate page-switch ghosting; add damping to entrances

1. Ghosting: switchPage did not await its (async) renderer, so the old page
   faded back in and was swapped out only when data arrived.
   -&amp;gt; switchPage is now async and awaits the renderer before fading in.

2. Damping: --ease-silk is now cubic-bezier(0.22, 1.18, 0.36, 1) -- a slight
   overshoot that settles back. Duration 0.68s, lift 12px, and all nine
   entrance animations use the silk curve.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
